            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0224" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1109: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-17T10:00:00+07:00">July 17, 1941—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. The following is the translation of a communication from the Governor General
                    of Indochina dated July 16, in reply to my most recent protest against the
                    continued seizures of American merchandise by the Japanese military authorities:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“With reference to my letter of July 8, 1941, I have the honor to advise
                            you that the Japanese mission has just informed me that it cannot alter
                            its first decision and that it will continue to remove the merchandise
                            in storage, in conformity with the orders of the Government at
                            Tokyo.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Cavite for repetition to the Department, Chungking, Peiping, Hong Kong,
                    Shanghai. Please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
